1. Creating Responsive Layouts
Mixins can be used to create responsive layouts that adapt to different screen sizes. For example, you can define a mixin that changes the number of columns in a grid system depending on the screen size:
// Define a mixin for a grid with 3 columns on desktop and 1 column on mobile
@mixin grid($columns) {
display: flex;
flex-wrap: wrap;
@media screen and (min-width: 768px) {
width: calc(100% / #{$columns} - 20px);
margin-right: 20px;
}
@media screen and (max-width: 767px) {
width: 100%;
}
}
// Use the mixin on a container element
.container {
@include grid(3);
}
This code defines a mixin for a grid system and uses it on a container element. The mixin changes the number of columns in the grid depending on the screen size, making the layout responsive.
