3. Create jQuery functions to handle the navigation controls. Bind click events to the `prev` and `next` buttons to move the slider back and forth between slides. Here's an example:
```
var slideCount = $('.slides').children().length;
var slideWidth = $('.slider').width();
var slideIndex = 0;
function showSlide(index) {
slideIndex = index;
$('.slides').css("transform", "translateX(-" + (slideIndex * slideWidth) + "px)");
}
